<doc id="164692" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=164692" title="Darunavir/cobicistat">
Darunavir/cobicistat

Darunavir/cobicistat, sold under the brand names Prezcobix (US) and Rezolsta (EU), is an &lt;a href="antiretroviral%20medication"&gt;antiretroviral medication&lt;/a&gt; used to treat and prevent &lt;a href="HIV/AIDS"&gt;HIV/AIDS&lt;/a&gt;. It is a &lt;a href="fixed%20dose%20combination%20drug"&gt;fixed dose combination drug&lt;/a&gt; containing 800 mg of &lt;a href="darunavir"&gt;darunavir&lt;/a&gt; and 150 mg of &lt;a href="cobicistat"&gt;cobicistat&lt;/a&gt;. Darunavir is an &lt;a href="HIV%20protease%20inhibitor"&gt;HIV protease inhibitor&lt;/a&gt; and cobicistat increases the effectiveness of darunavir by blocking its metabolism by the enzyme &lt;a href="CYP3A"&gt;CYP3A&lt;/a&gt;.
Darunavir/cobicistat was approved for use in the European Union in November 2014, and for use in the United States in January 2015.
